            ;;
        drop-unauthorized)
            cat <<'EOF'
egresslock drop-unauthorized PROFILE PORT

End connections on a port that the profile's policy no longer allows.

This is the recovery step printed when `disallow --direct` removes a
rule but cannot end the connections that used it. It reads the live
firewall rules, ends the connections on PORT that the policy no
longer allows (including connections to addresses the rule allowed
before a DNS refresh changed it), keeps the connections the policy
still allows, and reports success only after a fresh check finds none
